  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Work After Dark",
    "overview": "**Concept: Work After Dark.** Aekarut's real software is the light source in a quiet exhibition space. Visitors move through projects, not a grid of decorated cards. The first viewport pairs the name and role with two precisely aligned DroneAid screens; the gallery continues in depth behind them.\n\nRedesign decision: **Replace direction.** The Swiss Poster Series is superseded, including its flat-sheet, square-corner and category-plate rules. The earlier rejected dark card grid remains rejected. Dark is explicitly requested here; cards, chips and ornamental glows are not.\n\nFixed: static Astro/Vercel, real captured evidence, honest team credit, HTML text, direct project access, the approved personal details, complete non-3D access. Flexible: composition, light, framing, typography weights. Assumption: retain the already self-hosted Archivo rather than add a font download.\n\nPrimary aesthetic: restrained dark gallery. Layout: continuous spatial exhibition plus a compact index. Material: real device models in graphite (one phone, one monitor), dark stone-like plinths, untinted screens. Motion: camera translation with restrained pointer parallax, not perpetual spinning. Runner-up: glass-led full-canvas controls; declined because reflective chrome would compete with the work.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One continuous 3D space; the camera flies between projects as you scroll.",
      "Real captures as the light source: unlit screens on real phone and monitor models, standing on lit plinths.",
      "Every title, summary, caption and fact is real HTML.",
      "One phone size per page; pairs are symmetric.",
      "A complete still version for reduced motion, small or weak devices and no WebGL.",
      "Category colour only as small dots and plinth edge lines.",
      "Collection order: applications first, then studies and open-source work."
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "dos": [
      "Do show the artifact in the first viewport, keep exact screen aspect ratios and symmetric pairs.",
      "Do keep a direct route to every project and all facts in HTML.",
      "Do preserve natural scrolling, keyboard navigation, image zoom and source links.",
      "Do use category color sparingly and lighting only to explain physical depth."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't revive colored plates, the expanding column accordion, heavy condensed poster type or a dark card grid.",
      "Don't hide content for an entrance animation, draw text in WebGL, require a GPU, distort screenshots, or imply a prototype is a running production app.",
      "Don't use device models with brand marks or licences that need more than a credit; every model is credited in the footer."
    ]
  }
}
